			<div class="content" id="post-content-3574804">
									

<p>This is hella late but the idea basically came in two parts: firstly, the actual object and the plot that the object was attached to.</p>
<p>The object itself (the Joyce thesis) was either inspired by me going through various Modernist literature a few weeks back or someone talking about an idea they had in chat &#8212; I'm gonna guess kinch? Whatever the case, it stuck in my head long enough that I was planning to write about it in some form or another, but it was only recently that I actually found out just what I was gonna have it do, both with the effect and the plot.</p>
<p>The story kind of condensed out of thin air, in all honesty: I was irritated and thinking about Fifthists in an unrelated train of thought, and the closing sentence of the last note basically condensed out of thin air: &quot;Six layers deep. One to go. The well awaits.&quot; From there, I kinda had to work backwards for the rest of the plot points, and tied in a couple SCPs I enjoyed through tangential references or even as central plot points (3005, 2747 respectively.) Eventually I had to come up with a plot point that would drive the whole story, and the pattern-matching James Joyce thesis seemed like a pretty good thing to pair it with.</p>
<p>tl;dr Any time I come up with good ideas I have little to no hand in it.</p>

